---
import ServiceSection from "../components/ServiceSection.astro";
import Endpoint from "../components/Endpoint.astro";
import RustSchema from "../components/RustSchema.astro";
---

<ServiceSection id="service-s2master">
  <Fragment slot="title"><code>S2Ms</code> — SC2 master data</Fragment>
<p class="endpoint-index">
  <a href="#s2master-mmq-info">S2Ms/17 MMQGetInfo</a>
  <a href="#s2master-current-season">S2Ms/27 CurrentSeasonResponse</a>
  <a href="#s2master-mmq-list">S2Ms/28 MMQGetList</a>
  <a href="#s2master-site-latency">S2Ms/35 SiteLatencyInfo</a>
</p>
    <Endpoint id="s2master-mmq-info" direction="bidirectional" phase="protected" structure="mixed generated order" status="capture decoded">
      <Fragment slot="title"><code>S2Ms/17</code> S2Master::MMQGetInfo</Fragment>
      <p>Requests information for one matchmaker handle. The response correlates by
      token and optionally returns generated queue information.</p>
      <RustSchema code={`// client → server
struct MMQGetInfoRequest {
    token: u32,
    handle: MatchMakerHandle,
}

// server → client
struct MMQGetInfoResponse {
    generated_flag: bool,
    token: u32,
    queue_info: Option<QueueInfo>,
}`} />
      <p class="endpoint-note">The response's generated <code>QueueInfo</code>
      contains a 40-byte per-game block, static queue ID and flags, and a matchmaker
      handle. Capture evidence supplies that physical form; reflection supplies the
      top-level logical type.</p>
    </Endpoint>

    <Endpoint id="s2master-current-season" direction="bidirectional" phase="protected bootstrap" structure="generated order" status="verified">
      <Fragment slot="title"><code>S2Ms/27</code> S2Master::CurrentSeasonResponse</Fragment>
      <p>An empty request asks for the current season. The response returns either a
      16-bit error or the current authority, matchmaker, league, season, and
      league-configuration data.</p>
      <RustSchema code={`// client → server
struct CurrentSeasonRequest;

// server → client
struct CurrentSeasonResponse {
    result: CurrentSeasonResult,
}

enum CurrentSeasonResult {
    Success {
        authority_state: bool,
        ranked_matchmakers: Vec<RankedMatchmakerConfig>, // count: 7 wire bits
        leagues: Vec<League>,                           // count: 9 wire bits
        season_info: SeasonInfo,
        league_configurations: Vec<LeagueConfig>,       // count: 9 wire bits
    },
    Failure(u16),
}`} />
      <p class="endpoint-note">The generated order includes reserved runs and
      reordered nested members that are absent from logical metadata.</p>
    </Endpoint>

    <Endpoint id="s2master-mmq-list" direction="bidirectional" phase="protected" structure="generated order" status="capture decoded">
      <Fragment slot="title"><code>S2Ms/28</code> S2Master::MMQGetList</Fragment>
      <p>Lists matchmaker handles selected by a FourCC tag filter.</p>
      <RustSchema code={`// client → server
struct MMQGetListRequest {
    filter_tags: Vec<FourCC>, // count: 5 wire bits, maximum 16
    program_id: FourCC,
    token: u32,
}

// server → client
struct MMQGetListResponse {
    token: u32,
    result: Result<Vec<MatchMakerHandle>, u16>,
}`} />
      <p class="endpoint-note">The request surrounds its tag list with a generated
      20-bit prefix and one-bit suffix. These generated layout bits surround the
      logical filter values.</p>
    </Endpoint>

    <Endpoint id="s2master-site-latency" direction="client → server" phase="protected bootstrap" structure="generated order" status="capture decoded">
      <Fragment slot="title"><code>S2Ms/35</code> S2Master::SiteLatencyInfo</Fragment>
      <p>Reports measured latency and preference for each advertised game site.</p>
      <RustSchema code={`struct SiteLatencyInfo {
    sites: Vec<SiteLatency>, // count: 7 wire bits, maximum 64
}

struct SiteLatency {
    name: String,    // byte count: 6 wire bits, maximum 32
    wire_tag: Bits<3>,
    latency_ms: u32,
    preferred: bool,
}`} />
    </Endpoint>
</ServiceSection>
